            {
                "entry_id": "76ba1695-9054-3d6a-83b1-186781c8f5e3",
                "word": "sackful",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "cced5be1-407f-45e5-a0f9-bcd7bf628b5a",
                        "entry_id": "76ba1695-9054-3d6a-83b1-186781c8f5e3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sackfuls"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4535c21e-591e-4675-80c7-b38c8ee79cdc",
                        "entry_id": "76ba1695-9054-3d6a-83b1-186781c8f5e3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sacksful"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "898608f9-50b8-3b11-956f-c636f165c2e7",
                        "entry_id": "76ba1695-9054-3d6a-83b1-186781c8f5e3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The amount a sack will contain."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9e5ef81-5a78-4f39-a4c4-3b24ec10872c",
                                "sense_id": "898608f9-50b8-3b11-956f-c636f165c2e7",
                                "text": "A sackful of sand won't help the soil here much, but a dump truck full would."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3be2bfb6-dca1-42ad-9da5-65c807d98fc4",
                                "sense_id": "898608f9-50b8-3b11-956f-c636f165c2e7",
                                "text": "If I be not so rich, as to sowe almes by sackfulls, euen my Mite, is beyond the superfluity of wealth: and my pen, my tongue, and my life, shal (I hope) helpe some to better treasure, then the earth affoords them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6493accb-ae06-4f39-9a03-e86680eb1514",
                                "sense_id": "898608f9-50b8-3b11-956f-c636f165c2e7",
                                "text": "Potatoes were getting very scarce. If you got a sackful you could take them down to the cook-house and swap them for a water-bottleful of coffee."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "51e54bdc-c465-4ec1-9106-96b9af41c1b4",
                                "sense_id": "898608f9-50b8-3b11-956f-c636f165c2e7",
                                "text": "You live until you die, and it doesn’t matter how you go; dead’s dead. So why carry on like a sackful of sick cats just because Herb Clutter got his throat cut?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cceb07c4-7138-3a1b-b51f-888ec75881da",
                        "entry_id": "76ba1695-9054-3d6a-83b1-186781c8f5e3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large number or amount (of something)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bb124f9-f9f1-4e4e-857b-573f46171468",
                                "sense_id": "cceb07c4-7138-3a1b-b51f-888ec75881da",
                                "text": "what can the Pope say more for his sackfull of traditions?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50ae27f7-055d-4554-a49e-0fa6e70ec815",
                                "sense_id": "cceb07c4-7138-3a1b-b51f-888ec75881da",
                                "text": "[…] away we went home again fraught with a Sackful of news to tell our Master."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "abf87b22-880e-4554-8744-ac393230b30f",
                                "sense_id": "cceb07c4-7138-3a1b-b51f-888ec75881da",
                                "text": "1853, uncredited translators, German Popular Tales and Household Stories: Collected by the Brothers Grimm, New York: C.S. Francis, Volume I, 74. “The Fox and the Cat,” p. 381,\n[…] I understand a hundred arts, and have, moreover, a sackful of cunning!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "07aee246-0d54-43fa-997b-cdd7a23ea584",
                                "sense_id": "cceb07c4-7138-3a1b-b51f-888ec75881da",
                                "text": "Day and night the poor fellow raved, and always about that confounded orchid, the loss of which seemed to weigh upon his mind as though it were a whole sackful of unrepented crimes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "153d57e7-b806-4b41-9c79-0dfe456b6a12",
                                "sense_id": "cceb07c4-7138-3a1b-b51f-888ec75881da",
                                "text": "1986, Hanif Kureishi, “Bradford” in Granta 20, Winter, 1986, p. 163,\nHe received sackfuls of hate mail and few letters of support."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
